[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"MySQL Authentication Plugins and Password Management Tutorial"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Securing a MySQL database server starts with robust authentication mechanisms and proper password lifecycle management. MySQL supports a plugin-based architecture for authentication, allowing administrators to implement various security protocols ranging from standard native hashing to external authentication services like LDAP, PAM, and FIDO security keys."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding MySQL Authentication Plugins"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Authentication plugins verify user identity and determine how credentials are exchanged and stored. MySQL comes with several default plugins, and understanding them is crucial for setting up secure user accounts."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"mysql_native_password: The legacy authentication method based on SHA-1 hashing, retained primarily for backward compatibility."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"caching_sha2_password: The default authentication plugin in MySQL 8.0, utilizing SHA-256 hashing with caching for improved performance."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"sha256_password: Uses SHA-256 hashing without caching, requiring secure connections (TLS) for password transmission."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Creating Users with Specific Authentication Plugins"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"When creating a new user in MySQL 8.0, you can explicitly define which authentication plugin the account should use. Here is how to create a user with the default caching_sha2_password plugin:"},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"CREATE USER 'app_user'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED WITH caching_sha2_password BY 'StrongPassword123!';
GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON my_database.* TO 'app_user'@'localhost';"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Managing Password Policies"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"MySQL provides the validate_password component to enforce robust password complexity rules. This prevents users from selecting weak passwords that are vulnerable to dictionary or brute-force attacks."},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"To install and check the status of the password validation component, execute the following SQL commands:"},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"INSTALL COMPONENT 'file://component_validate_password';
SHOW VARIABLES LIKE 'validate_password.%';"},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"Configuring Password Expiration and History"},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"Enforcing periodic password rotation is a common compliance requirement. MySQL allows you to set global or per-account password expiration policies, as well as restrict password reuse."},{"order":17,"type":"code","text":"-- Set global password expiration to 90 days
SET GLOBAL default_password_lifetime = 90;

-- Set expiration for a specific user
ALTER USER 'app_user'@'localhost' PASSWORD EXPIRE INTERVAL 60 DAY;

-- Prevent reusing the last 5 passwords
ALTER USER 'app_user'@'localhost' PASSWORD HISTORY 5;"},{"order":18,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":19,"type":"paragraph","text":"By leveraging modern authentication plugins like caching_sha2_password, enforcing complexity rules through the validate_password component, and establishing strict rotation policies, you can significantly enhance the security posture of your MySQL database deployment."}]
